To prove the theorem, we use the following Theorem~5.5 in \cite{hoffman:Bernoulli}.

\begin{theor}
A uniform $d$-to-one endomorphism $(Y,S,\mu)$ is one-sidedly conjugated to the one-sided Bernoulli
$d$-shift if and only if there exists a generating function $f$ so that $(Y,S,\mu)$ and $f$ are
tree very weak Bernoulli.
\end{theor}
